{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id24829417"}, "name":{"label":"Ste C 81"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-20T03:27:56-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"1619061445"}, "title":{"label":"Incredible"}, "content":{"label":"This is the best todo app I've used. Beautiful interface with well thought out interactions. Extremely powerful but not complicated to use. Love the ability to use headings in projects (great for identifying different phases of a project). Also really nice the way you can just drag things around the screen (no complicated menu systems). Absolutely love it.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id31596389"}, "name":{"label":"a3suri"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-20T02:38:02-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1619020836"}, "title":{"label":"Fantastic! Best GTD App ever!"}, "content":{"label":"Intuitive, Powerful and Reliable and with the same decluttered feel as before. \nThis is the Porsche of GTD Apps, with a lot of hidden Power under the hood!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id105869117"}, "name":{"label":"stirmal"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-20T02:08:21-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1618995535"}, "title":{"label":"Inordinately good"}, "content":{"label":"This app is absolutely mad. Outperforms other to-do managers by a mile. Should be taught in UI/UX design classes.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id42486681"}, "name":{"label":"Semanjoe1"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-19T21:43:55-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1618752775"}, "title":{"label":"Rock solid todo app"}, "content":{"label":"I've tried dozens of todo apps but never felt so certain that this is the one for me. \n\nCuts through the clutter and compliments the Getting Things Done mentality but not too rigid and adding a more common sense, and great user experience approach. At the moment there isn't anything I would change and that's really unlike me.\n\nI have the Mac version and felt an instant release of pressure when using it, as I was able to easily get things off my mind in a system that I trusted. It just works and version 3 was really worth the wait.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id25347007"}, "name":{"label":"jayenndee"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-19T18:40:31-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1618588948"}, "title":{"label":"Polished, practical and nearly perfect"}, "content":{"label":"I'd always struggled a bit with Things 2; while I liked the idea the workflow seemed a bit clunky  times and never really clicked (too much tapping at fields and menus). As a result I ended up abandoning it after a few months. \n\nThings 3 changes all that; the interface is really polished and fluid and you can create new todos and move them around really easily. The redesigned interface lays out information clearly, and animations which both make the app a pleasure to use and highlight important information.  It's pretty much the most polished app I've used - every pixel and animation has clearly been obsessed over.\n\nNo app is perfect, though and there are a couple of things that I'd like to see, particularly:\n\n- A fully featured extension (at the moment it just adds the todo to the inbox which is fine but I'd like to select where they go).\n- Repeating to dos in projects: at the moment they exist in areas. I heard that this would be changed in a future update. \n- And finally the natural language entry box is a bit hidden. Had to read the manual to find it (pull down on the date selector to get  the entry box). \n\nTo do apps are a personal thing; what works well for me might be to rigid or too unstructured for someone else. Things is flexible enough to be used as a strict GTD app or more causally as a general list of things to do.  I've tried pretty much every major to do app, from Omnifocus to ToDoist and after a month or so of use (I was in the beta for a bit) Things is the one I'm going to stick with.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
